  "worked_solution": "Let's go through each of the options.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $1.$ However, it also contains a constant term. Therefore not all of its terms are of degree $1.$\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $3.$ However, it also contains a term ($3xy$) that is of degree $2.$ Therefore, not all of its terms are of degree $3.$\n\n- The function $h(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $5.$ It is a polynomial of degree $5,$ and all of its terms are of degree $5.$",
